# Git LFS for model artefacts.
#
# `models/*.pkl` matches one level only. A file placed in any subdirectory —
# `models/seed/model.pkl`, say — would fall outside it and enter git as an
# ordinary binary, and a fresh clone would then fail on a missing LFS object.
# That is what closed PR #196: the tracking is the delivery mechanism, not
# bookkeeping about it.
#
# The recursive pattern is here **before** anything moves, because attributes
# are applied at `git add` time. Files added under the old pattern and moved
# afterwards stay non-LFS until the history is rewritten.
models/*.pkl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
models/**/*.pkl filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
models/**/*.pth filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
